from pathlib import Path
import json,sys,subprocess,datetime
import pandas as pd,numpy as np,scipy
from mapping_extension import O,sha
A=json.loads((O/'VERIFIED_AUDIT.json').read_text());assert A['status']=='bounded_diagnostics_complete'
B=json.loads((O/'ALLELE_QC_AUDIT.json').read_text());assert B['status']=='allele_quality_complete' and B['all_selected_targets_reviewed']
T=json.loads((O/'CLASSIFIER_TRIAGE.json').read_text());F=json.loads((O/'INDEL_FLAG_SAMPLING_CONTEXT.json').read_text())
q=pd.read_csv(O/'reportable_quality_quantiles.tsv',sep='	');h=pd.read_csv(O/'reference/megablast_recovery/homology_summary.tsv',sep='	')
lines=['# NLGN4X expanded read/mapping diagnostic review','', 'This is a bounded stratified read review, not full-cohort read validation or independent genotype confirmation. All primary association estimates, genotypes and QC filters remain unchanged.','', '## Methods','', 'Before examining the new reads, selection was fixed among strict-eligible participants with called genotypes for all three targets. The design sampled ancestry, sex, case/control status and any-target-carrier strata by deterministic hash and retained eligible participants from the earlier pilot. Participant-level data and exact sample/cell counts remain inside Workbench.','', 'Primary mapped, nonduplicate, non-QC-failed, nonsupplementary reads were evaluated. High-quality allele summaries required MQ >=30, MQ <255 and BQ >=20; overlapping templates were counted once. Independent samtools-depth calculations were checked against the CIGAR parser for every target and selected participant. Reference MD5 and source identities were verified. The deletion classifier reconstructed a fixed local haplotype and accepted equivalent shifted CIGAR deletions.','', 'Fixed diagnostic flags were depth <10, target fraction >0.10 for noncarriers, <0.90 for homozygous/hemizygous carriers, outside 0.25–0.75 for heterozygotes, and GQ <20. They are descriptive flags; no participants were removed or association tests repeated.','', '## Reviewed read summaries','', 'All selected source records and all three targets per selected participant were verified; retrieval and depth cross-checks had no failures. Below, each reported subgroup and metric has more than 20 participants; exact denominators are withheld to avoid small-cell or complementary disclosure. Values are medians across participants, not participant counts.','', '| Target | Sex | Expected target fraction | GQ | Aligned-base depth | HQ template depth | HQ target fraction | MQ |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in q.loc[q.family.eq('sex_genotype')].itertuples():
 vals=[r.target, 'Male' if r.sex==1 else 'Female',r.expected_target_fraction,r.GQ_median,r.aligned_base_read_depth_median,r.HQ_template_depth_median,r.HQ_target_fraction_median,r.MQ_median_median]
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join(str(round(v,4)) if isinstance(v,(float,np.floating)) else str(v) for v in vals)+' |')
lines+=['','## Flags and interpretation','', 'Low-depth observations remain flagged. The two SNPs had no fixed allele-balance flags in this selected review. The deletion had heterozygote allele-balance flags, including flags persisting when the denominator was restricted to exact REF/ALT haplotypes; these are retained rather than dismissed as a classifier artifact. Post hoc binomial sampling and strand diagnostics provide context, not a replacement QC gate.','', 'Some reads had a mate aligned to chrY. No high-quality target-ALT read had a chrY mate or recorded alternative chrY alignment in the reviewed sample. Absence of such tags is not proof that no alternative alignment is possible.','', '## Reference-sequence context','', 'REF and ALT contexts with 50, 150 and 500 bp flanks were compared with the complete matching Broad reference, including chrX, chrY and other contigs. All 18 query summaries were verified for the MegaBLAST high-similarity recovery search with word size 28 and DUST seed masking. The unmasked BLASTN search hit its 1800-second limit and a DUST-masked BLASTN attempt hit its 600-second limit; both failures and partial outputs are retained. The high-similarity heuristic and seed masking improve tractability, but this is not an exhaustive search for diverged or low-complexity homology. The complete settings, sequence/reference provenance, alignments and per-query scores are retained. This reference-context search does not realign participant reads or certify whole-genome mappability.','', 'See reference/megablast_recovery/homology_summary.tsv for on-target and competing alignment scores. Competing alternate contigs may represent the same genomic locus and must not automatically be interpreted as unrelated loci.','', '## Implications and limits','', 'The diagnostic adds read-depth, allele-balance, mapping-quality, base-quality and strand evidence to the earlier genotype-field summaries. It does not establish that alignment artifacts have been excluded throughout the cohort. Deletion balance flags and the absence of orthogonal genotype confirmation remain explicit limitations. It provides no new independent replication and does not strengthen any P value. NLGN4X remains a model-sensitive candidate region.','', 'Independent replication requests were sent to BioVU and Dr Nick Dand on 18 September Pacific, asking first for feasibility, carrier adequacy and overlap assessment before new association results. No external cohort or independent result is yet secured.','']
assert len(h)==18 and h.on_target_coverage.ge(.99).all()
competing=h.other_locus_score_gap.dropna();assert competing.gt(0).all()
lines += ['## Verified reference-context findings','', 'All 18 expected chrX alignments covered the full query and scored higher than competing alignments returned by this high-similarity search. chrY homology is present: the 101-base rs183018930 REF/ALT contexts had chrY alignments of approximately 93.2% and 92.2% identity, respectively, with lower scores than the expected chrX alignment. Longer contexts also show X/Y similarity. This documents homology rather than excluding it, and is not an actual-read realignment test.','', '| Query | Expected X score | Y score | Y identity (%) | Y query coverage |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for _,r in h.fillna('-').iterrows():lines.append('| '+' | '.join(str(r.get(k,'-')) for k in ['query','on_target_bitscore','chrY_bitscore','chrY_identity','chrY_query_coverage'])+' |')
lines += ['', 'The earlier unmasked and DUST-masked BLASTN failures are preserved and were not silently treated as complete. The completed MegaBLAST diagnostic is limited to its high-similarity heuristic. The absence of an equal-scoring competing hit is not proof of unique mappability for every participant read.','']
(O/'Mapping_Review.md').write_text(chr(10).join(lines))
versions=dict(python=sys.version,pandas=pd.__version__,numpy=np.__version__,scipy=scipy.__version__,samtools=subprocess.check_output(['samtools','--version'],text=True).splitlines()[0],blastn=subprocess.check_output(['blastn','-version'],text=True).splitlines()[0])
manifest=dict(created_UTC=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),versions=versions,source_sha256={x.name:sha(x) for x in (O/'source').glob('*.py')},report_sha256=sha(O/'Mapping_Review.md'),read_audit_sha256=sha(O/'READ_AUDIT.json'),verified_audit_sha256=sha(O/'VERIFIED_AUDIT.json'),allele_audit_sha256=sha(O/'ALLELE_QC_AUDIT.json'),private_data_retained_in_Workbench=True,submission_or_export_approval=False)
(O/'FINAL_DIAGNOSTIC_MANIFEST.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2));print('MAPPING_REVIEW_AND_EXECUTED_SOURCE_MANIFEST_SAVED')

